    "updated_at": "2016-06-14T14:06:26Z",
    "body": "> This looks great, is your name already in the acknowledgments?\n\nYes, it's already there. :)\n\n> I wonder if we should look into integrating this tool into https://github.com/whatwg/html-build.\n\nmwic is not really suitable for automated use.\nIt produces copious amout of output, consisting mostly of false positives, which the user has to manually sweep through. (But it's designed to make this sweeping relatively painless.)\n\nspellintian (part of [Lintian](https://lintian.debian.org/)) or [codespell](https://github.com/lucasdemarchi/codespell) are better-suited for fully-automated spell-checking, although they would still require some fine-tuning to avoid false positives.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
